WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:02.510
Greetings.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:06.060
The fall days are very comfortable.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.350
How is your health?

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.290
I am doing well.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.990
Recently, there's been a change in my life.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.410
I have a new roommate in my cell.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.250
I'm not sure if he's pure evil or just a fool.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.740
One thing's for sure.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:27.830
He's the reason I'm able to continue writing letters to you.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.750
It won't be long before we are able to meet.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.750
I hope to tell you much about my roommate, my friend.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.340
I eagerly anticipate the day.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.010
Sincerely yours.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.000
<b>Everybody Loves Pajamas</b>

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.490
Hey, Gramps.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.860
Where's your partner?

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.250
Oh, he went to the restroom.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.540
What? I told you to always get permission and

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.930
accompany him to the restroom.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:46.580
Sorry, he's taking a dump, so I figured I shouldn't tag along.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.740
Oh, it's okay.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.300
Shachi needed to take a dump, so he tagged along.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.280
That's not the issue here.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.830
Oh, now I need to take a dump.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.350
Will you come with me, guard?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.310
Why?!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.950
Bro, if they find us,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.890
they won't even bother sending us to the disciplinary room.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:03.800
That's right.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.430
I want to go to the warden's room,

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.110
not the disciplinary room, Shake-kun.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.200
It's Shachi.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.330
We're going to find proof that he's breaking the law.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.670
Weren't you his pawn?

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.820
Show me the way, Hamachi-kun.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.800
It's Shachi!

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.450
It's impossible!

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.160
Do you realize how many locked doors we have to go through?!

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.310
Yes, this is Kamiya.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.060
What?! What are you doing, you idiot?!

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:26.060
Damn, did they find out that we ditched our work?

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:27.590
You lost the keys?!

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.060
Were they stolen?!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.650
I guess it wasn't us.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.850
We need to get back before we're caught.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.430
Grow a spine.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.000
They're busy looking for whoever stole the keys.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.120
They won't care about a couple fellows skipping work.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:40.900
Let's go.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.610
They're gonna care!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.320
Because the person who stole the keys is right here!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.120
Huh? Where?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.080
It's you! Why are you acting surprised?!

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.350
I didn't steal anything.

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.090
I just picked up the keys after someone dropped them.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.490
And I'm going to give them back.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.260
That doesn't make it okay!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.130
Bro, you're going all the way this time.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.610
Yeah, time for revenge, Itachi-kun.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:02.850
That's not even close to my name.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.740
Okay, let's disguise ourselves so we don't stand out.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.040
You're the man, Bro.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.950
You must have stolen clothes from the guards.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:11.950
Listen up.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.340
I'm a guard in pajamas.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.460
You're the prisoner I'm bringing in.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.630
Nothing's changed!

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.070
How are you a guard in pajamas?!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.920
The only difference is you're wearing a western style prison uniform

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:21.610
instead of an Asian one!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.620
Don't blame me.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.650
The guard was working a night shift so he had his pajamas on.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.370
Why was the guard wearing pajamas like that?!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.940
Hell, you might as well be naked!

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.360
Don't worry.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.750
If I put on a bandanna and carry a stick...

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.450
See? Don't I look like a guard in pajamas?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.220
Don't act like guards in pajamas are a common phenomenon!

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.580
Nobody's seen one before!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.010
Then I won't pretend to be a guard.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.500
I'm a pajama kid with a pillow and I don't believe in ghosts.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.120
Why would a pajama kid be walking around with a prisoner?!

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.810
And who cares if you believe in ghosts?!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.070
What's that in your right hand?!

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.070
What are we supposed to say if they find us?!

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.280
Hey! What are you guys doing?!

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.170
Why is a prisoner here with a pajama kid?!

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.070
What's going on?!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:02.910
Don't move!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.910
K-Keep it down!

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.830
Or this pajama kid is gonna get it!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.420
H-Help me pajama!

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:13.920
I see!

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.280
He's taken the pajama kid hostage so he can escape!

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.670
Wait, why is this pajama kid even here?!

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.810
Shut up! Everyone wants to be a pajama kid!

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.700
If you keep talking, these pajamas will be torn apart!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.430
Stop! Don't hurt the pajamas!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.430
Why are you a bad guy now?!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.290
Raise your hands! Outta the way!

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.150
Clear the path!

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.190
Listen to me.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.110
If you follow me, you know what's gonna happen!

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.830
These white lines will be completely red!

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.870
About face, then march!

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.950
Then go into the locker room and change into your pajamas!

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:46.490
Listen to me, if you button them wrong, you know what's gonna happen!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.640
G-Got it.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.950
Go!

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.530
We're on high alert!

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.920
Get the prisoners into their cells!

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.550
Were they really stolen?

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:02.960
I-I'm sorry...

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.180
Apologizing isn't going to help!

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.330
Where's the warden?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.230
Well, he's out right now.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.240
They've been found out...

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.430
Damn, why now?!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.140
Come in.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.290
This is the warden speaking.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.190
The warden?

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.190
Yes, I wanted everyone to gather in one place.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.690
Who are you?!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.650
You're not the warden!

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.700
I'm the warden.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:27.200
But I'm not feeling well,

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.950
so someone else is doing the talking for me.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.710
W-Warden!

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:40.460
Welcome to our land, guards.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.470
<b>Warden's Office</b>

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.970
This is bad, Bro!

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.460
We need to hurry!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.470
Damn! I can't find anything incriminating!

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:48.840
Bro!

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.020
I had the kids on the outside do some research.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:54.510
I gave them one of the letters the old man's been getting

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.730
and told them to check the address.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.660
Why are you bringing this up now, Bro?

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.680
They went to the address to see his son.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.410
But they didn't find him.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.760
He wasn't there?

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:06.490
No.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.220
And it wasn't just the wrong address.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.500
He's no longer in this world.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.650
You mean...

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:19.090
His son died ten years ago.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.250
Of disease.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:26.010
He's been writing letters to someone who will never get them.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.800
That would explain why he never got any responses.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:35.350
But at some point, he began to receive frequent replies.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.270
From someone who no longer existed...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.280
Who was it?!

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.690
Were those letters written by a ghost?!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.660
Our positions have been reversed, warden.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.110
Hey, warden.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.700
Looks like your own men hate you as much as the prisoners do.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.420
Hey, if you don't come out,

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:01.460
we'll take out all our stress on the warden!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.630
Watch closely.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.270
We're going to beat the warden to death!

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:08.970
Stop!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.980
Stop this nonsense. It's for your own good.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.730
Hey, unlock that door.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.740
Did you say something, old man?

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.820
For an old man who was stuck in prison for the rest of his life,

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.240
his son was the only light in his dark world.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:36.670
But it was an illusion.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.750
There was no light.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:43.740
But you couldn't take that away from him.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.840
When you're sitting behind bars, the whole world is an illusion.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.250
So he gave him what he could.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:57.410
That would explain why they only made small talk.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.020
<b>From your son.</b>

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.020
You're...

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:11.280
Bastards, you think you can get away with touching my toys?

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:15.760
I'm sending you all to the disciplinary room.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:25.150
I never imagined that the sick and twisted warden was

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.740
doing this for the old man.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:31.630
He pretended to be the old man's son to hide his death.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.420
If the old man is allowed to see his son,

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.390
these letters will have been for nothing.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:42.060
That's why he's been trying to get me to make trouble.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.820
To get his clemency revoked.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:47.530
Why would the warden do this?

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.400
Beats me.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:53.320
He probably doesn't know either.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.530
Attention, criminals!

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:04.510
Open the doors and release the guards at once!

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:08.050
Or else you will all have your sentences increased!

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.050
You're the ones who locked us up in here!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.050
We're just making ourselves comfortable!

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:17.670
Shit, they started a riot!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:20.680
The warden's wish came true in an unexpected way.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.880
The old man's clemency ain't happening now.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.010
That doesn't matter!

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.690
Those guys aren't gonna let the warden live!

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.830
The old man's in danger, too!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.040
Can't have that.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.830
If he dies, there won't be anyone to prove my innocence.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.580
Besides , I finally found evidence of his evil.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:42.330
I'll make him pay for the crime of fooling a weak old man.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.960
Bro, was that your goal from the beginning?

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.200
Thanks for the help.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.900
Now hide.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.220
If you mess around any more, they'll hang you.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:57.600
Wait, you were using me for your own petty reasons?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.350
It's my turn to use you.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.100
I don't give a damn about the old man or the guards.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:09.190
But I can't let our sentences be extended because of one stupid warden.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:11.500
I'll act as a decoy and draw the attention of the guards.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.620
Use that opening to deal with this riot.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.110
Wait, that's...

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:18.080
Go crazy and get some more time tacked onto your sentence.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:22.370
Then we can continue to have a blast in this place.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.960
Hey, wait!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.260
Hey, look!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.210
It's Shachi!

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.710
Get him!

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.960
Catch me if you can.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:37.150
But it won't be easy to grab the sleeve of the king of criminals!

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.220
Your sleeves were ripped off!

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.970
I'm counting on you, Bro.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.350
Yeah, I got this, Buri.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.230
It's Shachi!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:50.820
Damn! They used the commotion to run away!

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.350
Shachi's men aren't around either!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:55.980
Damn! If the hostages escape, we'll be crushed!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.130
Find them!

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:05.230
Warden, a lot of men have been injured.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.500
We need to get them medical care.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:09.750
Old man, hang in there. Hey, old man!

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.000
The prisoners want me.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.260
I'll hold them here.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.220
What?

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.340
But you'll be...

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.360
Are you trying to get yourself killed?!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.770
Give this to the old man.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:25.020
<b>Kuzunosuke Beri</b>

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.020
It's the last letter.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:28.650
Found ya.

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:32.270
Hey, what are you all doing here?

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:34.970
Move it!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:37.670
If you don't hurry, I'll throw you into the disciplinary room!

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.800
Warden! We'll be back with help as soon as we can!

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.030
Don't die!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:44.640
Warden!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.690
Greetings.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:49.500
I apologize that this isn't a letter from your son.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.280
If you are reading this letter,

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.060
it means that I have disappeared for one reason or another,

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.470
and you are no longer receiving letters from your son.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.570
However, you don't need to worry.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.350
Your son is doing fine.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:08.050
His work has taken him to another planet,

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.520
so it's difficult for him to send letters.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:13.590
There is a lot of paperwork that has to be done

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.650
before you can receive mail from another planet.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:21.200
I apologize that I was unable to continue delivering his letters.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.890
I'm sure that you no longer remember,

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.320
but when I was first assigned this position,

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.080
I was a complete outsider.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.090
After causing trouble everywhere I went,

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.860
my parents dumped me in prison.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:38.930
The hardened criminals weren't going

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:42.590
to listen to a clueless young fool,

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:47.440
and the guards resented me for my connections.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:54.310
I would often find myself going to the oldest prisoner, you.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.440
The rules of the prison,

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.100
methods for handling nasty prisoners,

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.820
the way to strike underhanded deals,

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.550
as well as the fact that the outside light was a ray of hope

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.020
for the prisoners in their dark cells...

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.380
I learned everything from you.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.880
I can't say that I'm a respectable member of society.

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:18.130
I'm aware that I have nothing to be proud of.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:22.050
However, you're the reason I'm able to stand

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.620
on my own, unsightly legs.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:28.660
All I could manage was to help deliver these letters.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.710
However, I would be happy to know that they gave you hope.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.030
There will be a significant delay before the next letter arrives,

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.770
but please don't forget that there is

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.370
someone outside who is thinking of you.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:47.230
Please remember that your son is not the only person

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.040
who cares about you.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.670
It was nice knowing you.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.790
From the evil prison warden.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.240
We finally shut him up.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.800
Hey, we're not finished with you yet.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.740
Excellent.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.310
It's your favorite place, the disciplinary room.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.810
<b>Disciplinary Room</b>

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.590
This will make the perfect tomb.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:12.860
Time to pay you back for all the abuse.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.790
Hey, I have something to tell you guys who are

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.570
never returning to society.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:29.390
When entering someone else's cell, knock first.

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:31.040
That's prison etiquette.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.720
Especially when you're entering the disciplinary room.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:37.330
There might be a really violent criminal inside.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.130
Son of a bitch!

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.300
B-Bastard...

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.190
Why are you here?

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.250
It's too early for you to die.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.140
You haven't met your father yet, you stupid son.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.100
Bastard...

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:55.190
Hey! Have you forgotten what he did to us?!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.520
I haven't forgotten.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.160
Let me handle this.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.610
You've blown off enough steam.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:03.570
If you still need some exercise, I'll be happy to take you on.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.920
Well, warden?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.070
Did you forget your promise to me?

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.830
If I make trouble, you'll set me free.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.460
Now, who's the most stressed out guy here?

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.490
Let's start the first Tournament of Stress!

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:18.830
Bring it!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.340
Welcome to my disciplinary room!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.840
Warden!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.840
Are you okay, Warden?

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:30.350
What? I don't see any of the prisoners who were rioting.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.730
Over there! There's a prisoner!

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:34.220
Why is he in a western uniform?!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.230
Hey, stop!

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.230
Where are you going?!

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:37.480
Enough.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:39.520
Warden!

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:41.580
Set him free.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:41.980
Huh?

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:46.490
These prison walls can't contain him.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:52.530
The prison's really calmed down.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.350
We got prison guards and prisoners sleeping next to each other.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.040
They all need to relax.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:03.310
Still, I'm surprised they haven't hanged us yet.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.730
That's the thing.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.840
I heard that we won't be punished.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:07.710
Huh? Why not?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.690
The warden isn't going to let us off.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.050
Didn't you hear? The warden...

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:20.020
I heard that you're going to shoulder the prisoners' crimes.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:26.550
I knew that it was risky to play with prisoners

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.110
since there are people like you.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.740
What I did was nothing compared to your letter business.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.030
You chose a kind illusion over harsh reality.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:38.580
Since you made that choice,

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:43.540
you're obligated to keep up the lie until the very end.

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:46.540
But you got scared

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.760
that he would eventually find out you were lying.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:53.510
So you gave up and ran away.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:57.180
As a result, the old man's being allowed to meet up with his son again.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:01.560
I no longer have the right to walk through this door.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.070
You don't have the right to whine either.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.410
You're supposed to be an evil warden.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:11.300
Tell the old man the harsh truth and laugh in his face,

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:13.930
or keep feeding him illusions until the day he dies.

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.340
One or the other.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.560
Make sure the old man knows your decision.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.830
And then I'll forgive you for throwing me in the slammer.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:26.840
Or else, I'll send your head flying and go back to jail.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:31.840
If I'm an evil warden, you're a demon.

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.340
The old man never told me

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:39.480
that it was so hard to give prisoners hope.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:43.180
I don't know what I'm doing anymore.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:49.090
True, you've been fooling the old man for a long time.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:53.490
You pretended to be his son and offered him false hope.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:58.570
But your feelings for the old man are no illusion.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:01.510
Come on. It's time for the meeting.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.710
Wait, I no longer...

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.470
No longer have the right to go in?

00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:07.840
That's not true.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.320
I have a criminal who's been

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:16.350
accused of falsifying documents and identity fraud!

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.650
O-Okay, get in here, maggot!

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:20.510
The victim is waiting in the visiting room,

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.790
you mother-licking insect!

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:24.850
Y-You bastards...

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:28.400
Yes, pajamas are the best.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:32.860
I don't see anything happening.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:41.330
Warden, time for some of the best prison role playing of your life.

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:44.900
Listen up, you have ten minutes.

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:46.370
Any longer and the chief will find out...

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:48.360
I mean, you're not allowed to meet any longer!

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:49.750
Got it?

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:59.530
Good grief.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:03.460
We have so many nasty-looking guards around now.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:11.030
I heard that you quit your job.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:13.290
Do you have another job yet?

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.410
No, I'm searching still.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:19.290
I see...

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.700
Well, I wish you the best of luck.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.380
Try not to get yourself called an evil warden again.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:32.590
Yeah...

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.550
Guard, we're finished.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.160
Huh? Already?

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.070
Wait, old man!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.720
I've been...

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.720
Don't say anything.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.400
We were able to make small talk, just like always.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.900
That's all I need.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:59.410
Old man, did you...

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.230
I read the letter.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:04.530
It was better than usual.

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:08.500
But your handwriting is still ugly.

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:14.920
<b>Kuzunosuke Beri</b>

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:14.920
Warden, I've always been writing letters to my son outside.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:21.630
A son who turned out to have a nasty personality,

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.930
but that foolish son of mine is dedicated to his job.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:29.440
I'm glad I was able to see you today.

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:36.350
Will you continue to write?

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.680
Yeah, I will.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.560
It's a promise.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:56.000
Yeah, whoever breaks the promise gets sent to the disciplinary room.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:21:58.730
Ow!

00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:44.990
<b>Next Episode: Speaking of Crossovers, Don't Forget About Alien vs. Predator</b>

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:42.470
Next week at this time:

00:23:42.470 --> 00:23:43.490
Sket Dance!

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:44.990
For real?!
